ET AI Concierge Architecture – Detailed Explanation


1. Overview

The system follows a multi-agent AI architecture where:

A central router distributes tasks
Specialized agents handle domain-specific logic
A large language model (LLM) powers reasoning
Memory and storage ensure personalization

2.  Components & Roles

 User Interface (Gradio Chatbot)
Entry point for user interaction
Accepts natural language queries
Displays AI-generated responses
 Router Agent (Brain of System)

Role:

Classifies user intent into 4 categories:
Welcome
Financial
CrossSell
Marketplace

How it works:

Uses Gemini LLM for classification
Routes query to correct agent
Specialized Agents
Welcome Agent
Handles onboarding
Profiles user:
Experience level
Goals
Risk tolerance
Financial Navigator

Provides:

Investment advice
Portfolio suggestions
Learning resources
Uses retrieved memory context
Cross-Sell Agent
Promotes premium ET products
Creates urgency
Drives conversions
 Marketplace Agent

Recommends financial services:

Loans
Insurance
Credit cards
Wealth management

3. Core AI Engine

Gemini 2.5 Flash (LLM)
Handles:
Reasoning
Text generation
Intent classification
FAISS Vector Database
Stores embeddings of conversations

Enables:

Context retrieval
Personalized responses
4.  Memory System

Types:

Vector Memory
Semantic search
Context-aware replies
JSON Memory
Stores user/session data
Metrics Storage
Tracks usage analytic

5.  Communication Flow

Step-by-step Flow:

User sends message
Router Agent classifies intent
Query routed to relevant agent
Agent retrieves memory (if needed)
LLM generates response
Response stored in memory
Sent back to user
6.  Tool Integrations
Gemini API → AI reasoning
FAISS → vector similarity search
Sentence Transformers → embeddings
Gradio → UI interface
Graphviz → architecture visualization

